IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spc-nouns`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, "Miscellaneous and supplementary"
-- (sections 11 to 14).
--
-- Only section 12(1) is a test the Act itself applies. Everything else here is a
-- direction to look at a Schedule, or a power to make regulations whose content is
-- not among the inputs. The tests of section 12(1) are encoded because the rest of
-- the Act is stated to be subject to regulations made under section 12: a case that
-- section 12(1) reaches is a case the Act's own rules may not decide (see
-- spc-part-entitlement.l4, `s 1(4) -- regulations or a pilot scheme may displace
-- the Act's rules for the case`).

§ `Miscellaneous and supplementary`

§§ `11 Administration`

-- Section 11 says Schedule 1 has effect and describes its three Parts. It creates
-- no relation and applies no test of its own; the Schedule's paragraphs are
-- encoded in spc-sch1.l4.
-- src:168 | Schedule 1 shall have effect and in that Schedule—
-- src:169 | Part 1 makes amendments to Part 1 of the Administration Act (claims for, and payments and general administration of, benefit);
-- src:170 | Part 2 makes amendments to Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (c. 14) (decisions and appeals); and
-- src:171 | Part 3 makes miscellaneous and supplementary provision.
-- (not encoded: section 11 is a signpost to Schedule 1)

§§ `12 Polygamous marriages`

-- Section 12(1): the section applies to a case where three things are all true.
-- src:173 | (1) This section applies to any case where—
-- src:174 | (a) a person (“the person in question”) is a husband or wife by virtue of a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy;
-- src:175 | (b) either party to the marriage has for the time being any spouse additional to the other party; and
-- src:176 | (c) the person in question, the other party to the marriage and the additional spouse are members of the same household.
@ref s 12(1) (src:173-176)
GIVEN case IS A Case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) -- section 12 applies to the case` case MEANS
        "(a) a person is a husband or wife by virtue of a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy;"
    ... case's `husband or wife by a marriage entered into under a law which permits polygamy`
    ... "(b) either party to the marriage has for the time being any spouse additional to the other party; and"
    ... case's `either party to the marriage has a spouse additional to the other party`
    AND "(c) the person in question, the other party to the marriage and the additional spouse are members of the same household."
    ... case's `person, other party and additional spouse members of the same household`

-- Section 12(2) to (4): regulations may provide for entitlement, for the credits,
-- for a different standard minimum guarantee, and for treating the income and
-- capital of the other party and the additional spouse as the claimant's; and may
-- displace or modify provisions of this Act; and may prescribe nil. All powers.
-- The regulations are not among the inputs, so a case within section 12(1) is
-- reported as "Not covered by this encoding", never decided.
-- src:177 | (2) Regulations under this section may make provision—
-- src:178 | (a) as to the entitlement of the person in question to state pension credit;
-- src:179 | (b) as to any guarantee credit or savings credit to which that person is entitled;
-- src:180 | (c) for prescribing a different amount as the standard minimum guarantee in the case of the person in question;
-- src:181 | (d) in a case where the person in question is the claimant, for treating the income and capital of the other party and of the additional spouse as income and capital of the person in question.
-- src:182 | (3) Any such regulations may provide—
-- src:183 | (a) that prescribed provisions shall apply instead of prescribed provisions of this Act; or
-- src:184 | (b) that prescribed provisions of this Act shall not apply or shall apply subject to prescribed modifications or adaptations.
-- src:185 | (4) Except in relation to the amount of the standard minimum guarantee, any power to prescribe amounts by virtue of this section includes power to prescribe nil as an amount.
-- (not encoded: section 12(2) to (4) are powers to make regulations)

§§ `13 Transitional provisions`

-- Section 13: the Secretary of State's power to make transitional provision, with
-- examples. The appointed day is "such day as the Secretary of State may by order
-- appoint". Not a rule for a person whose case arises long after the appointed
-- day, and no appointed day is among the inputs.
-- src:187 | (1) The Secretary of State may by regulations make such transitional provision, consequential provision or savings as he considers necessary or expedient for the purposes of, or in connection with,—
-- src:188 | (a) the coming into force of any of the state pension credit provisions of this Act; or
-- src:189 | (b) the operation of any enactment repealed or amended by any of those provisions during any period when the repeal or amendment is not wholly in force.
-- src:190 | (2) The provision that may be made by regulations under this section includes in particular—
-- src:191 | (a) provision for a person who attains or has attained the qualifying age on or before the appointed day and who immediately before that day is entitled to income support—
-- src:192 | (i) to be treated as having been awarded on, and with effect as from, that day state pension credit of an amount specified in or determined in accordance with the regulations; or
-- src:193 | (ii) to be treated as having made a claim for state pension credit; and
-- src:194 | (b) provision for an assessed income period under section 6 of such length as may be specified in or determined in accordance with the regulations (which may be longer than the maximum period provided for by section 9(1)) to have effect in the case of a person who attains or has attained the qualifying age on or before the appointed day.
-- src:195 | (3) In this section—
-- src:196 | “the appointed day” means such day as the Secretary of State may by order appoint;
-- src:197 | “the state pension credit provisions of this Act” means this Act other than section 18.
-- (not encoded: section 13 is a power to make regulations; the appointed day is not among the inputs)

